# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# Why (found live 2026-07-17): with core.autocrlf=true a Windows clone checks
# *.sh out as CRLF. bash launched INSIDE an MSYS/Git-Bash session tolerates
# that (text-mode mount strips \r), so the scripts appear healthy -- but the
# SAME bash.exe launched from a Windows process (python subprocess, skill_lib's
# `bash -lc`, CI runners) parses the raw bytes and dies with
#   syntax error near unexpected token `$'in\r''
# i.e. whether a launcher works depended on WHO launched it. LF-pinning
# removes the whole failure class.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
